| AT1    | Navigate to storage location following the optimized route.                                   | Sequential       | Storage Location        | 1                | Only one robot is executing the collection phase; navigation must follow the predetermined optimized route.                                                         |
| AT2    | Send a precise resource request message to the storage.                                        | Sequential       | Storage Location        | 1                | The robot must communicate the exact resource requirements before collection can proceed.                                                                             |
| AT3    | Wait for confirmation that the requested resources are ready for retrieval.                     | Sequential       | Storage Location        | 1                | Waiting ensures that the resource is available before proceeding to collection.                                                                                      |
| AT4    | Collect the retrieved resources from the storage.                                              | Sequential       | Storage Location        | 1                | Physical collection is necessary to acquire the resource for subsequent delivery.                                                                                    |
| AT5    | Monitor battery level during the collection phase.                                             | Sequential       | Storage Location        | 1                | Continuous battery monitoring is critical to detect low battery conditions promptly.                                                                                 |
| AT6    | Navigate back to the recharging station upon low battery detection.                             | Sequential       | Recharging Station      | 1                | Safe return to a recharging station is essential when battery levels drop below the threshold.                                                                       |
| AT7    | Reassign the remaining collection task to another robot.                                      | Sequential       | Recharging Station / Central Control | 1                | Reassignment ensures the mission continues without delay despite low battery issues.                                                                                  |
| AT8    | Navigate to the specified delivery location.                                                   | Sequential       | Delivery Location       | 1                | The robot must travel to the correct destination to deliver the resource.                                                                                             |
| AT9    | Deliver the collected resources to the requesting agent.                                      | Sequential       | Delivery Location       | 1                | Physical delivery is the core action of the delivery phase.                                                                                                           |
| AT10   | Confirm that the resources have been successfully delivered.                                   | Sequential       | Delivery Location       | 1                | Confirmation is necessary to validate that the delivery phase is complete.                                                                                            |
| AT11   | Monitor battery level during the delivery phase.                                               | Sequential       | Delivery Location       | 1                | Ongoing battery monitoring is essential to detect low battery conditions during delivery.                                                                            |
| AT12   | Return the resource to a designated checkpoint if battery is low.                               | Sequential       | Checkpoint              | 1                | Returning to a checkpoint ensures that the resource is not lost and can be safely handled by another robot if necessary.                                               |
| AT14   | Trigger an alert if the resource fails to reach the checkpoint.                                 | Fallback         | Delivery Location / Checkpoint | 1                | Alerting is required to notify the system of a failure in resource handling, prompting further intervention.                                                          |
| AT15   | Send a report to the sector manager regarding the checkpoint failure.                           | Fallback         | Delivery Location / Checkpoint | 1                | Reporting ensures accountability and enables corrective actions by the management in case of a critical failure.                                                       |

─────────────────────────────  
Summary of Logical Relationships

• G1 → G2, G3 [AND; Sequential]  
  Justification: The mission is complete only when both the collection (G2) and delivery (G3) phases are successfully executed.

• G2 → G2.1, G2.2 [Fallback]  
  Justification: The normal collection process (G2.1) is executed unless the battery level falls below 10%, in which case the fallback (G2.2) is initiated.

• G3 → G3.1, G3.2 [Fallback]  
  Justification: Normal delivery (G3.1) is used unless the battery level drops below 30%, triggering the fallback (G3.2) to handle low battery conditions.

• G2.1 → AT1, AT2, AT3, AT4 [Sequential]  
  Justification: Each collection task must occur in order to ensure the resource is properly collected.

• G2.2 → AT5, AT6, AT7 [Sequential]  
  Justification: All steps are necessary for safely managing a low battery during collection.

• G3.1 → AT8, AT9, AT10 [Sequential]  
  Justification: Delivery tasks must be performed in sequence to ensure successful resource handover.

• G3.2 → AT11, AT12 [Sequential] and fallback to (AT14, AT15) if AT12 fails  
  Justification: Battery monitoring and safe return to a checkpoint are critical; if the checkpoint return fails, an alert and report are required.

Disclaimer: The above goal model is a conceptual design intended to illustrate how the mission description can be decomposed into a hierarchical goal model with associated tasks. For implementation in safety-critical systems, further refinement and validation by domain experts are recommended.
